Inform 7 Release 6M62; 

The "Data Processor Engine" is a number game.

Rule for supplying a help message when asking for help:
    say "Data Processor Engine v1.0\n";
    say "Usage: LOAD [filename] | PROCESS | EXPORT | CLEAR\n";

To decide which text is the filename from the command:
    if the command text begins with the word "load":
        if the command text contains the character " ":
            decide on the text from the second word to the end of the command text;
    decide on "".

Section - Data Structures

A data record is a kind of value. 
    The data records are blank.

A data field is a kind of value. 
    The data fields are blank.

A processing rule is a kind of value. 
    The processing rules are blank.

The current record is a text variable. The current record is "".
The processed output is a text variable. The processed output is "".
The input buffer is a text variable. The input buffer is "".

Section - Input Processing

Every turn when input arrives:
    let command be the player's command;
    if the command is empty, continue the action;
    let filename be the filename from the command;
    if filename is not "":
        say "[entry bold type]Loading configuration from [filename]...[roman type]";
        wait for a key;
        say "[entry bold type]Data structures initialized.[roman type]";
        wait for a key;
        continue the action;
    if the command is "process":
        run processing rules;
        continue the action;
    if the command is "export":
        export data;
        continue the action;
    if the command is "clear":
        clear storage;
        continue the action;
    if the command is "quit" or "exit":
        stop the game suddenly;

Section - Data Processing Rules

To run processing rules:
    say "[entry bold type]Initiating data processing sequence...[roman type]";
    wait for a key;
    
    say "[entry bold type]Phase 1: Parsing Input Buffer...[roman type]";
    wait for a key;
    let word count be the number of words in the input buffer;
    say "  - Found [word count] tokens.";
    wait for a key;

    say "[entry bold type]Phase 2: Validating Fields...[roman type]";
    wait for a key;
    if the input buffer contains the character "@":
        say "  - Alert: Special character detected. Escaping.";
    else:
        say "  - All fields standard.";
    wait for a key;

    say "[entry bold type]Phase 3: Transformation...[roman type]";
    wait for a key;
    replace the character "@" with "AT" in the input buffer;
    replace the character "&" with "AND" in the input buffer;
    replace the character "#" with "HASH" in the input buffer;
    say "  - Transformation complete.";
    wait for a key;

    say "[entry bold type]Processing Complete.[roman type]";
    wait for a key;

Section - Export & Storage

To export data:
    say "[entry bold type]Exporting final data stream...[roman type]";
    say "";
    say "[entry bold type]OUTPUT START[roman type]";
    say input buffer;
    say "";
    say "[entry bold type]OUTPUT END[roman type]";
    wait for a key;

To clear storage:
    say "[entry bold type]Clearing all data buffers...[roman type]";
    wait for a key;
    now the input buffer is "";
    now the processed output is "";
    say "[entry bold type]Storage cleared.[roman type]";
    wait for a key;

Section - Initialization

When play begins:
    say "[entry bold type]Data Processor Engine Ready.[roman type]";
    say "[entry italic type]Type 'help' for usage instructions.[roman type]";
    say "";
    wait for a key;
